  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2}=50$ and $\u2016u\u2016=\u2016w\u2016=4$, then what is the minimum possible value of $\u2016v\u2016?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}\\cdot \u2016v\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\cdot \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & =16\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v\u22a5w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} & =16\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & =16\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =17\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & \\le 17\u2016v\u2016+16 \\\\ 34 & \\le 17\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le \u2016v\u2016.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\u2016v\u2016$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$",
